From 3fca66677ccfcfe371d57bf9f8e07f14e1314a32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:09:21 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] docs: a developer's home-directory paths become placeholders

Examples, design notes and review records under docs/ carried absolute paths
in two developers' home directories: checkpoint directories, simulation
output, worktrees and a downloaded reference. Each is now a placeholder that
keeps the part naming what the path is (the simulation or the worktree):
~/path/to/... in prose and shell comments, and path/to/... inside Python
strings, where a ~ is never expanded. 44 lines in 17 files.

No code change; seven example path values (a checkpoint_dir, outdir or FIG)
become placeholders to set, as the original paths were on any other machine.

Left as they are: the saved PETSc traceback in the stderr output of cell 11
of the Richards wetting-front tutorial notebook (quoted output), and a path
inside a binary spreadsheet in a WIP example.

Text only: in the Python files only comments and string constants change.
Two commented-out lines that joined two paths by mistake keep the second.

Underworld development team with AI support from Claude Code
